Package: ICONS
Title: Integrative Analysis of Covariance Matrices and Network Structure
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Yezhi", "Pan", email = "yezhipan7@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-4014-0302"))
Description: Detects interconnected community structure in a large covariance
    or correlation matrix with an adaptive greedy peeling algorithm, and uses
    the detected communities to specify the non-zero loadings of a
    semi-confirmatory factor analysis (SCFA) model.  All SCFA parameters --
    factor loadings, the covariance matrix of the common factors, error
    variances, and factor scores -- have closed-form maximum likelihood
    estimators that are uniformly minimum-variance unbiased, together with
    exact variance estimators for Wald inference.  Estimation never forms a
    p-by-p matrix, so the method scales to tens of thousands of observed
    variables.  Methods are described in Yang, Ma, Bi and Chen (2024)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2401.00624>, Yang, Chen and Chen (2024)
    <doi:10.1080/00031305.2024.2329681>, Chen, Zhang, Wu, Bi, Kochunov and
    Hong (2024) <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/kxad007>, and Wu, Huang, Culbreth,
    Waltz, Hong and Chen (2022) <doi:10.1111/biom.13537>.
